k, with no gradient of sunset colors (orange, pink, or purple) that would suggest dusk or twilight.\n- In later frames (9–10), the sky is fully black, confirming nighttime.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe visual evidence overwhelmingly indicates that these frames were captured **at nighttime**.\n\n- The transition from Frame 1 to Frame 10 shows a clear progression from late dusk (Frames 1–4, where some ambient sky light remains) to full night (Frames 9–10, with a black sky and all lighting artificial).\n- The narrator’s caption “after a few mins, im now here in Harajuku from Shibuya” suggests these frames are sequential and represent a short time span, likely capturing the transition from dusk into night.\n\n**Final Answer: Nighttime**'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-10 (10 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0981.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0982.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0983.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0984.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0985.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0986.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0987.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0988.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0989.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/RCAqKnvu_P0/frames/frame_0990.jpg\nVLM Response: Based on a detailed analysis of the 10 provided frames from Takeshita Street in Harajuku, the time of day can be determined by examining the lighting conditions, shadows, and ambient light.\n\n---\n\n**1. Natural daylight vs artificial lighting:**\n- The sky is no longer bright blue or even light gray; it is a deep, dark blue, indicating the sun has set.\n- All illumination in the scene comes from artificial sources: neon si